msgstr ""

#: src/Pro__premium_only/Reminders/RemindersModule.php:235
msgid "<p>Hi {{customer_name}},</p><p>unfortunately we still haven’t seen a payment for your order <strong>{{order_number}}</strong>. The payment deadline ends today.</p><p><strong>If the payment hasn’t reached us by {{grace_end_date}}, the order will be cancelled automatically</strong> and the goods released again.</p><h3>Your products</h3><p>{{items}}</p><h3>Payment</h3><p>{{payment_details}}</p><p>If you’ve already made the transfer, all good – the payment is probably on its way. If you no longer want the order, you don’t need to do anything.</p><p>Your order status: {{order_status_url}}</p><p>Best regards<br>your {{shop_name}} team</p>"
msgstr ""

#: src/Pro__premium_only/Reminders/RemindersModule.php:266
msgid "days after ordering, then daily at"
msgstr ""

#: src/Pro__premium_only/Reminders/RemindersModule.php:267
msgid "Time of the payment reminder"
msgstr ""

#: src/Pro__premium_only/Reminders/RemindersModule.php:268
msgid "o’clock"
msgstr ""

#: src/Pro__premium_only/Reminders/RemindersModule.php:269
msgid "If a prepayment order is still unpaid this many days after ordering, the customer gets a reminder with the payment details every day at the set hour from then on – until the order is paid, cancelled, or otherwise resolved (with auto-cancellation: until the end of the payment deadline, see below). A manual reminder (order list) counts as that day’s reminder. Time 6–20; sending happens during that hour. Text: Settings → Templates → “Payment reminder”. 0 days = no automatic reminder."
msgstr ""

#: src/Pro__premium_only/Reminders/RemindersModule.php:270
msgid "Auto-cancellation"
msgstr ""

#: src/Pro__premium_only/Reminders/RemindersModule.php:272
msgid "Automatically cancel unpaid prepayment orders (reason “not paid”)"
msgstr ""

#: src/Pro__premium_only/Reminders/RemindersModule.php:273
msgid "Grace period"
msgstr ""

#: src/Pro__premium_only/Reminders/RemindersModule.php:276
msgid "The grace period is a buffer after the payment deadline ends during which nothing happens: no emails, no cancellation. Bank transfers often take one to two business days, and the cashier still has to record the payment – this way nobody who paid on time gets cancelled."
msgstr ""

#: src/Pro__premium_only/Reminders/RemindersModule.php:277
msgid "Process: On the last day of the payment deadline, the customer gets the “Final payment reminder” with the cancellation date. Then it’s quiet for the grace period. If it’s still unpaid after that, the order is cancelled at the time of the payment reminder: the goods go back to the warehouse, the customer gets the cancellation email (noting that a payment already transferred will be refunded), and the cashier gets the internal cancellation email. Example with a 14-day deadline and 2-day grace period: final reminder on day 14, cancellation on day 17. An order is never cancelled before the final reminder has gone out and the grace period after it has expired."
msgstr ""

#: src/Pro__premium_only/Reminders/RemindersModule.php:282
msgid "on the day after the payment term, then every"
msgstr ""

#: src/Pro__premium_only/Reminders/RemindersModule.php:283
msgid "days again"
msgstr ""

#: src/Pro__premium_only/Reminders/RemindersModule.php:284
msgid "Same time as for the prepayment reminder. No cancellation, no “final reminder” – the goods are already with the customer. Text: Settings → Templates → “Invoice payment reminder”. 0 = remind only once."
msgstr ""

